[Music]  [Applause]  in Parkinson's often people can actually  walk but they lack the ability to  initiate walking we project the laser  lights in front of the opposing foot  the laser light will look like a line on  the floor in front of the wearer and  that can be used as an external cue for  the person to step across and in that  way continue walking  so this external cue can help people  trigger their ability to walk in a more  normal manner  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

